"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[43506],{743506:n=>{n.exports="# Kafka Streaming - SQL\n\nIngesting data from Apache Kafka using SQL in Spark Declarative Pipelines.\n\n---\n\n## Basic Kafka Ingestion\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE bronze_kafka_events AS\nSELECT\n  CAST(key AS STRING) AS event_key,\n  CAST(value AS STRING) AS event_value,\n  topic,\n  partition,\n  offset,\n  timestamp AS kafka_timestamp,\n  current_timestamp() AS _ingested_at\nFROM STREAM read_kafka(\n  bootstrapServers => '${kafka_brokers}',\n  subscribe => 'events-topic',\n  startingOffsets => 'earliest',\n  failOnDataLoss => 'false'\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Options\n\n| Option                                        | Description                                       | Example                         |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `bootstrapServers`                            | Kafka broker addresses                            | `'broker1:9092,broker2:9092'`   |\n| `subscribe`                                   | Topic(s) to subscribe                             | `'topic1'` or `'topic1,topic2'` |\n| `subscribePattern`                            | Topic pattern (regex)                             | `'events-.*'`                   |\n| `startingOffsets`                             | Where to start reading                            | `'earliest'`, `'latest'`        |\n| `failOnDataLoss`                              | Prevent failure if offsets expire                 | `'false'`                       |\n| `serviceCredential`                           | Unity Catalog service credential name             | `'my-credential'`               |\n| `kafka.ssl.endpoint.identification.algorithm` | SSL hostname verification (prevents MITM attacks) | `'https'`                       |\n| `kafka.request.timeout.ms`                    | Request timeout (prevents hanging connections)    | `'60000'`                       |\n| `kafka.session.timeout.ms`                    | Consumer session timeout (controls rebalancing)   | `'30000'`                       |\n| `kafka.group.id`                              | Consumer group ID (for offset tracking)           | `'my-consumer-group'`           |\n\n---\n\n## Parse JSON Payload\n\n### With Explicit Schema\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE silver_events AS\nSELECT\n  from_json(\n    event_value,\n    'event_id STRING, event_type STRING, user_id STRING, timestamp TIMESTAMP, payload MAP<STRING, STRING>'\n  ) AS data,\n  kafka_timestamp,\n  _ingested_at\nFROM STREAM bronze_kafka_events;\n```\n\n### Flatten Parsed Data\n\n```sql\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE silver_events_flat AS\nSELECT\n  data.event_id,\n  data.event_type,\n  data.user_id,\n  data.timestamp AS event_timestamp,\n  data.payload,\n  kafka_timestamp,\n  _ingested_at\nFROM STREAM silver_events;\n```\n\n---\n\n## Multiple Topics\n\n### Subscribe to Multiple Topics\n\n```sql\nFROM STREAM read_kafka(\n  bootstrapServers => '${kafka_brokers}',\n  subscribe => 'orders,customers,products',\n  startingOffsets => 'latest'\n)\n```\n\n### Use Topic Pattern\n\n```sql\nFROM STREAM read_kafka(\n  bootstrapServers => '${kafka_brokers}',\n  subscribePattern => 'prod-events-.*',\n  startingOffsets => 'latest'\n)\n```\n\n### Route by Topic\n\n```sql\n-- Bronze: all events\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE bronze_all_events AS\nSELECT * FROM STREAM read_kafka(\n  bootstrapServers => '${kafka_brokers}',\n  subscribe => 'orders,customers',\n  startingOffsets => 'latest'\n);\n\n-- Silver: orders only\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE silver_orders AS\nSELECT * FROM STREAM bronze_all_events\nWHERE topic = 'orders';\n\n-- Silver: customers only\nCREATE OR REFRESH STREAMING TABLE silver_customers AS\nSELECT * FROM STREAM bronze_all_events\nWHERE topic = 'customers';\n```\n\n---\n\n## Authentication\n\n### Service Credential (Recommended)\n\nUnity Catalog service credentials are the preferred authentication method for Kafka on Databricks. They eliminate JAAS configuration, work on shared clusters and serverless compute, and handle credential lifecycle automatically. Supported for AWS MSK, Azure Event Hubs, and GCP Managed Kafka.\n\n```sql\nFROM STREAM read_kafka(\n  bootstrapServers => '${kafka_brokers}',\n  subscribe => 'events',\n  serviceCredential => '<service-credential-name>'\n)\n```\n\nWhen using a service credential, the following options are **not needed**: `kafka.sasl.mechanism`, `kafka.sasl.jaas.config`, `kafka.security.protocol`, `kafka.sasl.client.callback.handler.class`.\n\n### SCRAM-SHA-256 Authentication\n\nSCRAM-SHA-256 uses challenge-response authentication and never transmits passwords in cleartext, making it more secure than SASL/PLAIN. Use this when service credentials are not available. Not supported by Azure Event Hubs — use SASL/PLAIN with `$ConnectionString` for Event Hubs.\n\n```sql\nFROM STREAM read_kafka(\n  bootstrapServers => '${kafka_brokers}',\n  subscribe => 'events',\n  `kafka.security.protocol` => 'SASL_SSL',\n  `kafka.sasl.mechanism` => 'SCRAM-SHA-256',\n  `kafka.sasl.jaas.config` => 'kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka.common.security.scram.ScramLoginModule required username=\"{{secrets/kafka/username}}\" password=\"{{secrets/kafka/password}}\";',\n  `kafka.ssl.endpoint.identification.algorithm` => 'https'\n)\n```\n\n### SASL/Plain Authentication\n\n```sql\nFROM STREAM read_kafka(\n  bootstrapServers => '${kafka_brokers}',\n  subscribe => 'events',\n  `kafka.security.protocol` => 'SASL_SSL',\n  `kafka.sasl.mechanism` => 'PLAIN',\n  `kafka.sasl.jaas.config` => 'kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka.common.security.plain.PlainLoginModule required username=\"{{secrets/kafka/username}}\" password=\"{{secrets/kafka/password}}\";'\n)\n```\n\n### Azure Event Hubs (Kafka API)\n\n```sql\nFROM STREAM read_kafka(\n  bootstrapServers => '${eventhub_namespace}.servicebus.windows.net:9093',\n  subscribe => '${eventhub_name}',\n  `kafka.security.protocol` => 'SASL_SSL',\n  `kafka.sasl.mechanism` => 'PLAIN',\n  `kafka.sasl.jaas.config` => 'kafkashaded.org.apache.kafka.common.security.plain.PlainLoginModule required username=\"$$ConnectionString\" password=\"{{secrets/eventhub/connection-string}}\";'\n)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Pipeline Parameters\n\nDefine Kafka configuration in pipeline settings:\n\n```yaml\nconfiguration:\n  kafka_brokers: broker1:9092,broker2:9092\n```\n\nReference in SQL:\n\n```sql\nbootstrapServers => '${kafka_brokers}'\n```\n\n---\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Add ingestion metadata:**\n\n```sql\nSELECT\n  *,\n  current_timestamp() AS _ingested_at,\n  topic AS _source_topic,\n  CONCAT(topic, '-', partition, '-', offset) AS _message_id\nFROM STREAM read_kafka(...)\n```\n\n2. **Parse in silver layer** - Keep bronze raw for reprocessing\n\n3. **Handle schema evolution** - Use permissive parsing with error handling\n\n4. **Monitor lag** - Check offset progress in pipeline metrics\n\n---\n\n## Common Issues\n\n| Issue                 | Solution                                                  |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Connection refused    | Verify `bootstrapServers` and network access              |\n| Authentication failed | Check secrets and JAAS config syntax                      |\n| No data received      | Verify topic exists and has data; check `startingOffsets` |\n| Lag increasing        | Check downstream processing bottlenecks                   |\n"}}]);
